liblocation where location-ui, location-control's schema or MCE are not
there (FreeBSD has no MCE; location-ui runs only inside a Hildon session,
started by hildon-session, and location-control's schema is loaded at boot
by rc.d/hildon_setup):

- location-ui shows the disclaimer and the "enable positioning" dialogs
  and answers with a "response" signal; with it running, liblocation asks
  it as on Leste. Only when no location-ui runs at all (the service unknown:
  no session, an unattended test) the start used to end in "System
  error"; then the dialog's yes is taken (the disclaimer accepted and
  stored in GConf, GPS and network positioning on), with a message.
- location-control's schema gives the device in GConf's method pair
  (com.nokia.Location, las); without it, the internal receiver ("las":
  gpsd through location-daemon) instead of a Bluetooth one, which needed
  BlueZ.
- MCE's get_device_mode tells flight and offline mode, in which liblocation
  restricts the methods. Without MCE the device mode is "normal".

